{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Test-failure triage complete for the post-rebase make test run (10 failed / 18000 passed / 61 skipped).\n\nRoot causes identified for all 10 failures:\n\n1. 2x tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py (test_committed_baseline_matches_live_surface, test_default_invocation_runs_the_check): expected. rebar.__version__ bumped 0.12.0->0.13.0 but tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json wasn't regenerated. This drift gate (commit 7383663d4a39) postdates the 0.12.0 release, so this is the first release cut since it existed. Confirmed via 'python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update' that ONLY the __version__ value changed in the baseline (git diff shows a single 1-line value change). Regenerated the baseline and will fold it into the release commit. Also updated docs/releasing.md step 1 to document this as a required release step going forward, so future releases don't rediscover it.\n\n2. 8x remaining failures (5x tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py, 1x tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py, 2x tests/interfaces/test_tracker_footprint_cli.py): CONFIRMED ENVIRONMENTAL, not a regression. Root cause: this session's shell environment has GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=3 / GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=safe.bareRepository / GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=explicit injected (by the CLI harness/sandbox), which makes 'git -C <bare-repo> ...' (used by these tests fixtures against bare tickets-remote.git repos) fail with 'fatal: cannot use bare repository ... safe.bareRepository is explicit', exit 128. Verified two ways: (a) reproduced identically on a clean, unmodified origin/main checkout with no version bump, ruling out a release-caused regression; (b) unsetting the 6 injected GIT_CONFIG_* env vars makes all 35 tests in these 3 files pass (35 passed in 24s). This matches the GIT_CONFIG_* injection issue noted as environmental in the 0.12.0 release ticket. Re-running make test now with those env vars unset to get a clean baseline before proceeding to commit."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788025963011819001,"uuid":"c301408d-33c3-4db5-8755-ebaf9fc50968"}